WEBVTT

00:01.001 --> 00:02.336
[♪ theme music playing]

00:24.316 --> 00:26.944
WOULD YOU MARRY ME?

00:29.029 --> 00:30.739
ALL CHARACTERS, PLACES,
ORGANIZATIONS, ETC. ARE FICTIONAL

00:30.822 --> 00:32.199
CHILD ACTORS WERE FILMED
WITH GUARDIANS PRESENT

00:32.282 --> 00:33.951
ANIMALS WERE FILMED
UNDER EXPERT SUPERVISION AND WELFARE RULES

00:36.703 --> 00:37.746
[chuckles softly]

00:39.540 --> 00:41.917
Can I get a copy
of my marriage certificate?

00:42.000 --> 00:43.460
[clerk] Sure, just a moment.

00:44.253 --> 00:45.254
[sighs]

00:46.129 --> 00:47.130
[keyboard clacking]

00:47.965 --> 00:50.008
[adjuster] Submit your
marriage certificate

00:50.092 --> 00:51.635
with the divorce date indicated.

00:51.718 --> 00:53.011
Then you can change the beneficiary.

00:53.095 --> 00:54.179
[sighs softly]

00:55.305 --> 00:56.306
Thank you.

00:59.726 --> 01:01.270
PROOF OF MARRIAGE

01:02.437 --> 01:03.730
SPOUSE: YOO MERI

01:03.814 --> 01:05.107
Where's the date?

01:07.276 --> 01:09.570
Where does it show
the date I got divorced?

01:12.698 --> 01:15.200
It looks like the divorce decree
wasn't submitted.

01:15.284 --> 01:17.202
-What?
-The divorce date gets finalized

01:17.286 --> 01:19.413
only after you hand in the divorce decree.

01:21.373 --> 01:22.749
You're saying

01:22.833 --> 01:25.294
-I'm not divorced yet?
-No.

01:25.377 --> 01:26.920
[♪ dramatic music playing]

01:27.004 --> 01:28.005
[inhales deeply]

01:29.006 --> 01:30.632
She didn't hand it in yet?

01:30.716 --> 01:31.717
Why not?

01:34.011 --> 01:35.304
Was she too busy?

01:37.472 --> 01:39.766
[sighs] But she can't be that busy...

01:40.767 --> 01:42.644
[♪ dramatic sting]

01:44.438 --> 01:45.439
Is she still...

01:48.900 --> 01:50.569
-[tires screech]
-[chuckles]

01:51.236 --> 01:54.364
Man, was she testing me or what?
[clicks tongue]

01:55.699 --> 01:58.577
She loved me so much
that she couldn't hand in the decree?

01:59.119 --> 02:02.497
You really can't take a woman's word
at face value.

02:03.457 --> 02:04.666
Come on, Yoo Meri.

02:04.750 --> 02:05.834
[sighs]

02:13.467 --> 02:14.468
[chuckles softly]

02:14.551 --> 02:17.179
[passerby 1] It's nice to come out
for an evening stroll.

02:17.262 --> 02:18.597
[passerby 2] It is. [gasps]

02:18.680 --> 02:19.681
Is this the house?

02:19.765 --> 02:22.684
[passerby 1] Yes, they're newlyweds,
and the wife won the lucky draw.

02:22.768 --> 02:24.770
[gasps] The husband got lucky.

02:24.853 --> 02:28.482
He needs to revere her forever.
Do you know how much a unit costs now?

02:28.565 --> 02:31.068
-He won the lottery.
-Oh, what great luck.

02:31.151 --> 02:32.861
-Oh, I'm so envious.
-She won it?

02:33.403 --> 02:35.197
[scoffs] What's that about?

02:38.116 --> 02:40.243
[realtor] Oh, and apparently,
Beauté Department Store

02:40.327 --> 02:44.539
even gave away one of these units
as a prize for newlyweds.

02:44.998 --> 02:45.999
Hang on.

02:49.544 --> 02:51.797
"Beauté Palace lucky draw."

02:52.422 --> 02:54.174
BEAUTÉ PALACE LUCKY DRAW

02:54.257 --> 02:55.592
BEAUTÉ PALACE

02:55.676 --> 02:57.344
[♪ gripping, dramatic music playing]

02:57.427 --> 02:59.763
BEAUTÉ 30TH ANNIVERSARY RAFFLE
WRAPS UP SUCCESSFULLY

03:01.640 --> 03:02.641
Meri?

03:07.104 --> 03:08.605
Is this that punk?

03:11.191 --> 03:12.359
They're newlyweds?

03:13.985 --> 03:15.070
You live here?

03:15.612 --> 03:18.031
You lost everything
in that rental scam, so how are you...

03:19.533 --> 03:20.742
Is your name also Wooju?

03:21.118 --> 03:24.371
-That's what Meri called you.
-Yes, unfortunately.

03:25.455 --> 03:26.790
How dare they?

03:28.667 --> 03:30.293
-[doorbell chimes]
-[door keypad beeps]

03:30.377 --> 03:31.461
You got here so fast.

03:31.795 --> 03:33.630
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

03:37.426 --> 03:38.593
Waiting for someone?

03:38.677 --> 03:40.011
I have nothing to say to you.

03:41.847 --> 03:43.432
I told you I'm done with you.

03:44.307 --> 03:46.393
I'm reporting you
to the police for stalking.

03:47.978 --> 03:49.563
I should be the one reporting you.

03:52.023 --> 03:53.191
[scoffs]

03:54.151 --> 03:55.527
PROOF OF MARRIAGE

03:55.986 --> 03:57.195
Did you have fun so far?

04:00.323 --> 04:01.491
The fake newlywed life.

04:01.575 --> 04:03.034
[♪ music increases in tempo]

04:16.923 --> 04:18.049
[scoffs softly]

04:22.095 --> 04:23.138
What a nice place.

04:23.638 --> 04:25.390
To think you won it in a draw.

04:26.641 --> 04:27.726
Good for you, Meri.

04:29.186 --> 04:30.604
How long were you going to dupe me?

04:31.146 --> 04:33.106
I never meant to dupe anyone.

04:33.190 --> 04:34.649
I couldn't reach you--

04:34.733 --> 04:35.859
That's your excuse?

04:35.942 --> 04:37.360
It's the truth.

04:37.444 --> 04:39.571
I kept calling you to tell you
I won the house

04:39.654 --> 04:41.239
but you ignored me.

04:43.033 --> 04:45.368
So, you found a guy to replace me?

04:45.452 --> 04:48.330
I had no choice.
They'd cancel my win without a husband.

04:50.499 --> 04:52.459
I had to pay back
the money I'd lost on the scam.

04:52.542 --> 04:53.585
[scoffs]

04:55.212 --> 04:57.047
The win's canceled if you're divorced.

04:57.964 --> 04:58.965
PROOF OF MARRIAGE

04:59.049 --> 05:00.634
That's why you didn't finalize it?

05:01.092 --> 05:03.804
Wow, you got pretty brazen.
Enough to pull a con.

05:04.888 --> 05:06.264
Weren't you a bad liar?

05:06.348 --> 05:08.642
You cheated on me
and made me a divorcée overnight,

05:08.725 --> 05:10.602
leaving me with all the debt.

05:12.771 --> 05:13.897
[clears throat]

05:17.275 --> 05:18.318
What a joke.

05:21.154 --> 05:22.280
[breath trembling]

05:25.242 --> 05:26.493
[in English] Okay.

05:27.118 --> 05:28.703
[in Korean] We can't change the past.

05:29.120 --> 05:30.664
Let's be future-oriented.

05:31.706 --> 05:32.958
End it with that punk.

05:33.625 --> 05:34.960
-What?
-You don't need a fake

05:35.043 --> 05:36.586
now that the real one is back.

05:38.129 --> 05:39.297
What's wrong?

05:39.381 --> 05:41.091
He's just some client.

05:42.133 --> 05:44.052
Did you actually fall for him?

05:44.803 --> 05:46.513
[♪ poignant, melancholy music playing]

05:50.892 --> 05:51.893
Why won't you answer?

05:53.520 --> 05:54.521
Yoo Meri.

05:54.604 --> 05:55.814
Answer me.

06:00.110 --> 06:02.362
If that's what it's like,
I must do something.

06:02.445 --> 06:05.115
I'll call the department store
and make sure you both pay.

06:05.198 --> 06:06.908
-Go ahead.
-What?

06:06.992 --> 06:08.743
I was going to come clean anyway.

06:09.870 --> 06:12.789
I panic dozens of times a day,
scared that I'll get caught.

06:14.624 --> 06:15.625
I regretted it all.

06:16.626 --> 06:19.462
I thought I could spend
the rest of my life free of worry

06:19.546 --> 06:21.214
if I had a house like this.

06:23.049 --> 06:24.509
But I can't sleep in peace.

06:26.678 --> 06:29.389
I'll struggle with the guilt
every single day.

06:30.515 --> 06:32.142
What's the point in having a house?

06:35.395 --> 06:37.480
And I feel guilty for what I did to him.

06:39.524 --> 06:40.525
I feel ashamed.

06:42.694 --> 06:44.237
-I'll end it all--
-Hey.

06:45.196 --> 06:46.740
Who says you can end it?

06:46.823 --> 06:48.199
I won't let this slide!

06:48.283 --> 06:50.243
You can come clean,
but I won't let you off.

06:50.827 --> 06:51.828
[scoffs]

06:52.370 --> 06:53.913
He's the grandson of Myungsoondang's CEO.

06:54.497 --> 06:56.041
The company's pretty popular.

06:56.124 --> 06:58.293
His grandma won the President's Award.

06:58.960 --> 07:01.671
What if word were to get out
that the heir had a fling

07:01.755 --> 07:04.257
with a married woman
and pretended to be her husband?

07:04.341 --> 07:06.092
Not only will he not inherit the company,

07:06.176 --> 07:08.094
I bet he'll have to leave the country.

07:09.137 --> 07:11.056
He'll be branded forever...

07:12.390 --> 07:14.517
-for being a fraud.
-Leave him out of it.

07:16.394 --> 07:17.646
He just...

07:18.521 --> 07:20.190
He helped me because I asked him to.

07:20.273 --> 07:21.816
I pleaded with him.

07:21.900 --> 07:23.568
-He had no choice--
-So, end it

07:23.652 --> 07:25.403
unless you want to see him go down!

07:26.237 --> 07:27.989
Or I'll bury him.

07:31.076 --> 07:32.077
Hey.

07:33.036 --> 07:34.120
Think carefully.

07:35.747 --> 07:37.040
Don't push me too far.

07:46.800 --> 07:47.842
[Meri gasps]

07:54.808 --> 07:55.850
[door opens]

07:57.852 --> 07:58.895
[door slams shut]

08:00.105 --> 08:01.189
[sighs wearily]

08:03.274 --> 08:04.359
Hi, Ms. Yoo.

08:04.859 --> 08:07.654
I'm at a coffee shop nearby.
Do you want anything to drink?

08:08.905 --> 08:10.115
Mr. Kim.

08:11.032 --> 08:12.075
I'm really sorry.

08:13.451 --> 08:16.079
I don't feel well all of a sudden.

08:16.162 --> 08:17.247
Are you ill?

08:17.330 --> 08:18.748
Should I get you some medicine?

08:18.832 --> 08:20.625
[Meri] No, I'll be fine.

08:20.709 --> 08:22.836
-I'll just rest.
-[acknowledges]

08:24.337 --> 08:26.506
Rest up, then.

08:27.173 --> 08:30.218
I'll cancel tomorrow's appointment
with Mr. Baek.

08:30.301 --> 08:31.678
We can meet some other time.

08:32.512 --> 08:33.513
Bye.

08:33.888 --> 08:35.432
[♪ melancholy music playing]

08:35.515 --> 08:39.185
-[line disconnects]
-[inhales deeply, exhales]

08:39.269 --> 08:41.396
Was she hurt by what Grandma said?

09:06.463 --> 09:09.382
WOULD YOU MARRY ME?

09:09.466 --> 09:10.467
EPISODE 9

09:10.592 --> 09:11.593
[knock at door]

09:17.265 --> 09:19.893
-Are you still up?
-Yes.

09:21.978 --> 09:24.981
I can't seem to sleep because of this.

09:25.607 --> 09:26.858
What?

09:26.941 --> 09:28.443
What is this?

09:28.526 --> 09:29.819
Do you remember Mr. Ko,

09:30.945 --> 09:32.739
who died in an accident
about two months ago?

09:33.448 --> 09:35.033
-Yes.
-That Mr. Ko

09:35.116 --> 09:37.077
kept these papers in a drawer at home.

09:37.994 --> 09:39.496
From what Ms. Kim found out,

09:39.579 --> 09:44.334
our company funds have been going
to J Consulting in the US.

09:45.543 --> 09:48.922
It looks like Mr. Ko realized that
and kept the papers.

09:52.383 --> 09:54.385
Did they embezzle from us, then?

09:54.803 --> 09:58.181
What is this J Consulting anyway?

09:58.264 --> 10:02.685
We hired them to help us
enter the US market.

10:02.769 --> 10:05.855
They helped us get the necessary licenses.

10:05.939 --> 10:08.399
[Kim Wooju] It looks like they managed
the local subcontractors, too.

10:08.483 --> 10:10.318
All our money went through them.

10:10.401 --> 10:14.114
Most of the subcontractors are
shell companies that exist in name only.

10:14.197 --> 10:15.198
[♪ tense music playing]

10:15.281 --> 10:16.366
What?

10:16.616 --> 10:18.118
It doesn't feel right.

10:18.535 --> 10:21.830
I'd like you to look into it
without Director Jang knowing.

10:23.289 --> 10:25.291
Director Jang hired the company.

10:26.459 --> 10:27.544
J Consulting, I mean.

10:39.848 --> 10:40.932
[sighs]

10:41.015 --> 10:42.559
J Consulting?

10:44.352 --> 10:46.855
What do they have to do with my uncle?

10:46.938 --> 10:48.940
CONSULTANT FEE

10:55.864 --> 10:57.282
J Consulting COMPANY FINANCIALS

11:00.201 --> 11:01.369
[Hangu exclaims]

11:02.370 --> 11:03.413
My documents...

11:05.498 --> 11:07.292
J Consulting America COMPANY FINANCIALS

11:07.375 --> 11:08.710
[♪ tense, gripping music playing]

11:09.460 --> 11:12.213
This is the document
that was on Uncle's desk.

11:13.214 --> 11:14.799
It's fine now.

11:14.883 --> 11:16.176
[Kim Wooju] Oh, okay.

11:17.760 --> 11:19.220
Why did he hide this from me?

11:30.815 --> 11:32.025
[line ringing]

11:36.279 --> 11:37.947
-[line connects]
-[in English] Hey, John.

11:38.615 --> 11:41.326
Can you do me a favor
and check out something for me?

11:42.619 --> 11:43.620
Yes.

11:44.120 --> 11:46.206
It's called J Consulting.

11:48.333 --> 11:49.334
All right.

11:49.792 --> 11:50.919
Thanks, I owe you one.

11:52.128 --> 11:53.296
Okay, bye.

11:54.631 --> 11:55.715
[line disconnects]

11:58.009 --> 11:59.719
J Consulting...

12:01.971 --> 12:05.350
[Songhee] Then we'll go
with what you chose.

12:05.767 --> 12:08.478
And we'll send you the revised invoice.

12:08.561 --> 12:09.604
Bye.

12:11.731 --> 12:12.732
[line disconnects]

12:12.815 --> 12:15.443
That was Ms. Oh. They loved our work...

12:18.029 --> 12:19.155
Ms. Yoo.

12:20.782 --> 12:21.783
Ms. Yoo.

12:23.493 --> 12:26.037
-Yes?
-Myungsoondang confirmed the design.

12:26.120 --> 12:28.414
Oh, that's great.

12:28.915 --> 12:32.835
Place the printing order
and send the revised design, too.

12:32.919 --> 12:34.045
Okay.

12:35.505 --> 12:36.839
Is something wrong?

12:36.923 --> 12:40.843
You skipped lunch,
and you don't look well.

12:41.344 --> 12:44.305
It's just that I didn't sleep well.

12:46.015 --> 12:47.308
I need some coffee.

12:59.195 --> 13:00.196
[coffee machine beeps]

13:03.283 --> 13:04.742
[coffee machine whirring]

13:06.244 --> 13:07.954
[Wooju] He's the grandson
of Myungsoondang's CEO.

13:08.496 --> 13:10.623
What if word were to get out
that the heir had a fling

13:10.707 --> 13:13.501
with a married woman
and pretended to be her husband?

13:13.584 --> 13:15.670
Not only will he not inherit the company,

13:15.753 --> 13:17.755
I bet he'll have to leave the country.

13:18.381 --> 13:20.091
He'll be branded forever...

13:20.800 --> 13:22.010
for being a fraud.

13:22.093 --> 13:23.136
[sighs]

13:23.219 --> 13:24.595
[♪ poignant, melancholy music playing]

13:28.891 --> 13:29.934
[coffee machine beeps]

13:32.895 --> 13:35.189
[Philnyun] Once you start lying,
it's easy to lie again.

13:36.774 --> 13:40.111
A one-time cheater can easily turn
into a career criminal.

13:44.157 --> 13:45.908
[in Korean] She might still be bothered.

13:48.077 --> 13:49.704
How can I make her feel better?

13:52.040 --> 13:53.916
-[sighs]
-[coffee machine beeps]

13:57.754 --> 13:58.921
[sighs]

13:59.756 --> 14:04.302
[Eungsoo] There are three surefire ways
to win a woman's heart.

14:04.385 --> 14:08.431
If she's upset or you need to make up
for a misunderstanding,

14:08.514 --> 14:09.974
this is incredibly effective.

14:10.600 --> 14:14.771
Then you can use this strategy
even after she becomes your girlfriend?

14:14.854 --> 14:15.897
You bet.

14:16.856 --> 14:18.066
Number one.

14:18.149 --> 14:20.485
It must be a feast for the eyes.

14:20.568 --> 14:21.986
-[Wonseok] "The eyes."
-[Eungsoo] Right.

14:22.070 --> 14:23.654
What should you do, then?

14:23.738 --> 14:26.199
Take her to a place
that will make her eyes pop open.

14:26.282 --> 14:27.784
[Wonseok] Such as...

14:27.867 --> 14:30.661
[Eungsoo] I'm making things
way too easy for you.

14:31.162 --> 14:32.497
Okay, why not?

14:32.580 --> 14:33.956
[♪ whimsical music playing]

14:34.040 --> 14:35.249
A place like this.

14:35.792 --> 14:37.001
Or like this.

14:37.085 --> 14:39.712
Can you resist the urge
to take photos at such a place?

14:39.796 --> 14:42.131
[Wonseok laughing] You can't.

14:42.590 --> 14:45.093
Can you share this list with me?

14:45.176 --> 14:48.179
I don't usually share
these things with anyone,

14:48.262 --> 14:51.641
but I will especially for you, Mr. Han.

14:51.724 --> 14:55.186
I'll shoot you the link.

14:55.269 --> 14:56.604
-[phone vibrating]
-It's sent.

14:56.687 --> 14:58.481
[Wonseok] I got the link.

14:58.564 --> 14:59.732
Thanks so much.

14:59.816 --> 15:01.943
[sucks teeth] What's the second trick?

15:02.026 --> 15:04.195
[Eungsoo] You must please her taste buds.

15:04.278 --> 15:07.949
When a woman speaks less
or is annoyed for no reason,

15:08.032 --> 15:10.451
feed her something.

15:10.535 --> 15:12.703
"I'm not hungry." Feed her anyway.

15:12.787 --> 15:14.413
And stay on guard.

15:14.497 --> 15:17.375
No matter how full they are,
they can keep on eating.

15:17.458 --> 15:18.709
It's quite scientific.

15:18.793 --> 15:22.547
Three rounds of desserts
after a full meal?

15:22.630 --> 15:24.006
Totally possible.

15:24.090 --> 15:25.508
Isn't it shocking?

15:25.591 --> 15:26.968
[Wonseok] Round one,

15:27.051 --> 15:28.219
round two,

15:28.302 --> 15:29.595
-round three.
-Yes.

15:29.679 --> 15:31.556
[Eungsoo] Draw a star
next to "stomach can expand."

15:31.639 --> 15:32.974
[Wonseok] "Stomach can expand, star."

15:33.057 --> 15:34.308
STOMACH CAN EXPAND

15:34.809 --> 15:36.018
What's the last one?

15:36.102 --> 15:37.103
Okay.

15:37.186 --> 15:41.774
The last one could be
the watershed moment.

15:41.858 --> 15:43.067
The last point.

15:48.030 --> 15:51.159
Make sure there's something in the hands.
[exclaims]

15:52.535 --> 15:54.036
[Wonseok] Oh, the hands.

15:54.120 --> 15:55.413
Hands?

15:55.496 --> 15:56.497
Hands?

15:56.581 --> 15:58.624
Why are you so self-centered?

15:58.708 --> 16:00.877
Not your hands, Mr. Han.

16:00.960 --> 16:03.504
-[Wonseok] Then what...
-A present.

16:03.588 --> 16:05.715
Get her a present, Wonseok.

16:05.798 --> 16:07.300
Sorry. I got carried away.

16:07.383 --> 16:08.467
A PRESENT

16:08.551 --> 16:09.969
-[Wonseok] A present.
-[Eungsoo] Yes.

16:10.428 --> 16:11.429
A present.

16:14.015 --> 16:16.601
[gasps] My gosh. Mr. Kim.

16:17.476 --> 16:18.561
[Kim Wooju clears throat]

16:21.147 --> 16:23.232
What did he write down?

16:28.237 --> 16:30.198
MYUNGSIK

16:30.781 --> 16:32.074
[phone vibrating]

16:39.290 --> 16:41.292
MYUNGSIK

16:48.799 --> 16:49.842
Hello?

16:49.926 --> 16:53.554
An amusement park or a famous restaurant
on the outskirts is fine, too.

16:54.138 --> 16:56.140
Do you want to go somewhere
or eat something?

16:56.974 --> 17:00.394
I might have to work this weekend.

17:02.188 --> 17:06.317
I need to work on the souvenirs
for the 80th anniversary.

17:06.400 --> 17:08.236
When do we go on a date, then?

17:08.861 --> 17:12.240
We barely talk
because you're always working late.

17:13.324 --> 17:14.575
[♪ soft, gentle music playing]

17:14.659 --> 17:16.410
Let's meet after the anniversary event.

17:16.911 --> 17:17.912
Okay.

17:17.995 --> 17:20.456
[clicks tongue] I should just
get back to work, then.

17:21.582 --> 17:22.625
[sighs]

17:22.708 --> 17:23.918
Poor me.

17:25.962 --> 17:26.963
Okay, then.

17:27.630 --> 17:29.882
Be sure to eat on time and take breaks.

17:30.967 --> 17:31.968
Bye.

17:43.604 --> 17:46.107
[sighs wearily]
She still sounds pretty down.

17:47.984 --> 17:49.277
-[clicks tongue]
-[phone vibrates]

17:51.070 --> 17:52.738
YOU HAVE A NEW EMAIL

17:53.573 --> 17:54.574
[exclaims quizzically]

17:59.745 --> 18:01.622
MARKETING TEAM

18:01.706 --> 18:03.374
-[Kim Wooju hums thoughtfully]
-[mouse clicks]

18:08.129 --> 18:09.797
[John in English]
J Consulting has closed down.

18:09.880 --> 18:11.799
The address you gave me is a parking area

18:11.882 --> 18:14.719
for a restaurant called "Route 66 Eats."

18:15.094 --> 18:16.762
Since the address matched perfectly,

18:16.846 --> 18:20.433
I looked up if the owner
was the same person, and it was.

18:20.516 --> 18:21.767
Her name is Jessica.

18:21.851 --> 18:23.019
She's an immigrant from Korea,

18:23.102 --> 18:25.980
-and her Korean name is Oh Minjeong.
-"Oh Minjeong"?

18:26.063 --> 18:28.649
I confirmed that
she has an eight-year-old son.

18:28.733 --> 18:31.944
She has been running this grill restaurant
in LA for a few years now.

18:32.028 --> 18:33.362
[♪ tense, gripping music playing]

18:33.446 --> 18:34.864
The address is the same?

18:37.325 --> 18:38.659
Jessica...

18:41.037 --> 18:42.455
CEO: Jessica

18:42.538 --> 18:43.539
Jessica.

18:45.374 --> 18:46.876
Jessica...

18:49.211 --> 18:51.464
[Miyeon] Thank you. Bye. [chuckles]

18:51.547 --> 18:52.757
[inhales, clears throat]

18:54.175 --> 18:55.593
[sighs]

18:55.676 --> 18:59.013
Jeez, do they take me for an idiot?

18:59.096 --> 19:01.766
They just say whatever they want
because they can.

19:01.849 --> 19:04.018
They don't know anything
about reading fortunes.

19:04.894 --> 19:07.271
Hi, darling. Are you free?

19:08.189 --> 19:12.485
The fortune-teller said
someone would betray me.

19:12.568 --> 19:15.071
It'd be someone close
and I should buy a paper talisman.

19:15.154 --> 19:16.405
My gosh.

19:16.781 --> 19:18.658
Do they think they can dupe me?

19:18.741 --> 19:21.535
Didn't you stop going to fortune tellers
after Eungsoo went to college?

19:21.619 --> 19:23.204
Why did you go back there?

19:23.287 --> 19:26.123
[Miyeon] Because nothing seems
to work out these days.

19:27.375 --> 19:29.377
But I'm really bothered

19:30.795 --> 19:32.171
by this betrayal thing.

19:34.006 --> 19:35.257
Could it be...

19:35.883 --> 19:36.884
my mom?

19:38.427 --> 19:39.428
Your mother?

19:41.180 --> 19:44.642
I got into a huge fight with her recently.

19:45.059 --> 19:49.355
She might announce that Wooju's her heir
at the 80th anniversary event.

19:49.438 --> 19:51.023
That would be a massive betrayal.

19:52.024 --> 19:55.152
Your mother must have a plan.

19:55.695 --> 19:57.613
And why would you argue with an elder?

19:57.697 --> 19:59.740
What if she faints or something?

20:00.825 --> 20:03.119
She keeps aggravating me.

20:03.202 --> 20:04.578
[chuckles softly]

20:04.662 --> 20:05.913
Don't let it get to you.

20:06.497 --> 20:08.916
I'm more worried about how you feel.

20:09.542 --> 20:10.751
I'll be home soon.

20:12.253 --> 20:13.379
Bye.

20:14.213 --> 20:15.965
-[chuckles]
-[line disconnects]

20:23.222 --> 20:26.684
Aren't you being too sweet
when you'll leave her soon?

20:28.936 --> 20:29.937
Are you jealous?

20:30.020 --> 20:33.482
[scoffs] More like a hint of suspicion?

20:35.568 --> 20:38.904
You act out of character sometimes
when you talk to her,

20:38.988 --> 20:39.989
and it's confusing.

20:40.072 --> 20:41.073
That's impossible.

20:41.782 --> 20:42.992
Don't mind her.

20:43.451 --> 20:45.453
I can't do that if you don't cooperate.

20:47.163 --> 20:49.707
Will you divorce her when you go back?

20:49.790 --> 20:52.334
I told you it's not yet time.

20:52.418 --> 20:53.669
Do it right away.

20:55.463 --> 20:56.464
Get a divorce.

20:56.547 --> 20:58.090
What got into you now?

20:59.175 --> 21:00.885
You managed to wait this long.

21:00.968 --> 21:02.136
[sighs wearily]

21:02.219 --> 21:03.721
[♪ tense music playing]

21:04.889 --> 21:06.599
How much longer do I need to wait?

21:07.391 --> 21:09.852
You can't take Henry to a mall
or a Korean restaurant

21:09.935 --> 21:11.228
in case someone recognizes you.

21:12.188 --> 21:13.481
We've been living like that
for eight years.

21:14.648 --> 21:15.649
No.

21:16.317 --> 21:17.401
Has it been 27 years?

21:18.402 --> 21:22.031
Did you forget what I did for you
for the sake of love and--

21:22.114 --> 21:23.199
Okay, I get you.

21:24.408 --> 21:25.409
I'm sorry.

21:26.535 --> 21:28.204
I'm sorry I wasn't considerate.

21:28.996 --> 21:30.247
We're almost there.

21:30.873 --> 21:33.876
Very soon, we'll have all we dreamed of.

21:35.294 --> 21:36.587
Hang in there.

21:42.968 --> 21:44.762
[sighs] I'm sorry.

21:44.845 --> 21:47.097
I get so anxious sometimes.

21:47.181 --> 21:48.265
I need you...

21:49.558 --> 21:52.770
to look after me
so I don't have to feel like that.

21:52.853 --> 21:53.938
[chuckles softly]

21:54.939 --> 21:56.023
I will.

21:59.944 --> 22:01.153
[doorbell rings]

22:01.987 --> 22:03.113
That must be Henry.

22:13.874 --> 22:14.875
[Jessica] Henry.

22:17.044 --> 22:18.504
Did you have fun surfing?

22:18.587 --> 22:20.339
[in English] Yeah, it was fun.

22:20.422 --> 22:21.465
[chuckles softly]

22:24.051 --> 22:25.135
[exclaims quizzically]

22:25.219 --> 22:26.262
Daddy?

22:26.345 --> 22:27.346
[in Korean] Dad's here.

22:27.429 --> 22:28.681
Dad!

22:31.976 --> 22:32.977
Thanks for picking him up.

22:34.228 --> 22:37.022
Oh, that's fine. I'll get going.

22:37.106 --> 22:38.107
Wait.

22:40.109 --> 22:42.403
-Here's some gas money.
-No, it's fine.

22:42.486 --> 22:44.613
I'm on my shift at the restaurant anyway.

22:44.697 --> 22:45.698
It's okay.

22:45.781 --> 22:47.074
Take it.

22:47.157 --> 22:51.036
You know I ask you to get Henry
because you can keep a secret, right?

22:54.707 --> 22:55.708
Thank you.

23:08.554 --> 23:09.763
[phone vibrates]

23:09.847 --> 23:11.682
MYUNGSIK

23:14.435 --> 23:17.104
[Kim Wooju] Ms. Yoo. Let's have a meeting.

23:18.147 --> 23:19.148
[Meri] Right now?

23:25.237 --> 23:26.614
[Kim Wooju] Yes, it's urgent.

23:29.283 --> 23:32.411
-Did we send the revised invoice?
-Yes.

23:32.828 --> 23:34.038
Did they say anything?

23:34.121 --> 23:35.497
Well, not yet.

23:35.581 --> 23:37.333
They'll call after their next meeting.

23:38.125 --> 23:39.126
Why?

23:45.132 --> 23:47.801
I need to go to Myungsoondang.

23:48.636 --> 23:50.346
[♪ soft, gentle music playing]

24:02.691 --> 24:03.901
[car horn honks]

24:19.458 --> 24:20.709
[kid giggling]

24:29.051 --> 24:31.762
Who says all meetings should be indoors?

24:32.805 --> 24:33.889
Let's get to it.

24:35.057 --> 24:37.393
What's all this about?

24:37.476 --> 24:38.477
You should sit.

24:47.861 --> 24:49.238
You skipped lunch, didn't you?

24:50.656 --> 24:51.699
The first agenda.

24:52.408 --> 24:54.243
I checked the invoice.

24:54.326 --> 24:56.912
Management okayed it, so you can proceed.

24:57.246 --> 24:58.247
[acknowledges]

24:58.330 --> 24:59.373
Okay.

25:06.088 --> 25:07.089
[sighs contentedly]

25:09.049 --> 25:10.050
The second agenda.

25:11.802 --> 25:13.887
What bothers you so much?

25:16.890 --> 25:19.560
You've been down
ever since we visited my grandma.

25:20.978 --> 25:21.979
Was it...

25:23.105 --> 25:24.773
because of what she said?

25:27.651 --> 25:30.779
That's just her old business philosophy.

25:31.155 --> 25:33.073
She didn't say that to spite you,

25:34.408 --> 25:37.244
and you were cornered
due to your circumstances.

25:38.203 --> 25:39.747
I'll talk to her for you.

25:41.707 --> 25:42.708
So, don't worry.

25:44.084 --> 25:46.587
[Wooju] So, end it unless you want
to see him go down!

25:47.838 --> 25:49.506
Or I'll bury him.

25:49.590 --> 25:51.508
[♪ poignant, melancholy music playing]

25:52.634 --> 25:55.637
We all have our circumstances.

25:57.431 --> 26:00.517
You told me so
on our way to the prize ceremony.

26:01.477 --> 26:03.854
Who in this world
doesn't have a sob story?

26:03.937 --> 26:05.939
But not everyone scams others like you.

26:07.024 --> 26:08.067
Back then--

26:08.150 --> 26:11.695
If I claim that what I did was wrong
back then but not anymore...

26:13.864 --> 26:17.284
everyone will call me a fraud, except you.

26:18.035 --> 26:21.038
You said you'd go to Beauté
and tell the truth

26:21.538 --> 26:22.873
and return the house.

26:23.999 --> 26:26.752
I'm thinking of not doing that now.

26:28.295 --> 26:30.214
I can turn my life around.

26:30.297 --> 26:32.007
I just have to keep it up
for one more month.

26:33.717 --> 26:37.971
I won't have to worry about money
for the rest of my life.

26:39.348 --> 26:40.432
To be honest,

26:41.225 --> 26:43.393
people all dupe each other.

26:43.811 --> 26:45.729
If I take the plunge,

26:46.647 --> 26:49.024
I won't have a worry
for the rest of my life.

26:49.108 --> 26:50.442
[chuckles softly]

26:50.526 --> 26:52.236
-Ms. Yoo.
-There's more.

26:53.779 --> 26:56.949
Will coming clean
improve my chances with you?

26:58.534 --> 27:00.285
How can we convince the chairwoman?

27:01.286 --> 27:05.207
How could I ever bear
your family's resentment?

27:07.292 --> 27:10.003
I don't want to tiptoe around others.

27:10.587 --> 27:12.881
You can't give up without even trying.

27:14.716 --> 27:16.718
I said I'd talk to my grandma.

27:17.302 --> 27:19.179
Can't you trust me on this?

27:20.305 --> 27:23.600
Watching you struggle
in the middle of us all

27:24.601 --> 27:26.562
would be too much for me.

27:30.274 --> 27:34.236
What are you saying?

27:38.574 --> 27:40.158
Do you want us to break up?

27:42.536 --> 27:43.579
Yes.

27:45.372 --> 27:46.415
Let's break up.

27:51.169 --> 27:52.212
I should go.

27:56.091 --> 27:58.093
[♪ sentimental pop music playing]

28:27.289 --> 28:28.957
[♪ ethereal sparkle]

28:35.797 --> 28:36.840
Well...

28:37.716 --> 28:39.551
Maybe it's because I like you.

28:41.470 --> 28:43.347
I don't like seeing you with another guy.

28:46.850 --> 28:49.227
[pounding heartbeats]

28:49.311 --> 28:50.979
UNDER THE LONELY SKY (English Ver.)

29:01.573 --> 29:02.574
[insect chirping]

29:04.242 --> 29:06.453
-You're totally my ideal type.
-[giggles]

29:15.712 --> 29:16.797
[♪ ethereal sparkle]

29:21.051 --> 29:22.928
[♪ sentimental pop music continues]

29:42.698 --> 29:43.699
[phone vibrates]

29:44.908 --> 29:46.827
MYUNGSIK

29:49.913 --> 29:51.456
[Kim Wooju] I know it's hard on you.

29:52.165 --> 29:54.459
I should've cared more about how you felt.

29:54.543 --> 29:55.544
I'm sorry.

29:56.503 --> 29:57.671
Get some rest today.

29:58.338 --> 29:59.715
Let's talk some other time.

30:00.632 --> 30:01.675
I'll wait.

30:08.890 --> 30:10.100
[breath trembling]

30:10.934 --> 30:12.102
[sniffling]

30:16.231 --> 30:20.110
[man] You know how cold and dark it is
at 4 a.m. in the winter.

30:20.652 --> 30:23.989
She'd change the coal briquette
while trying not to wake the kids,

30:24.489 --> 30:26.616
but the briquette
always got stuck to the side.

30:27.868 --> 30:29.494
You don't know much about coal, do you?

30:30.328 --> 30:31.371
I don't.

30:31.747 --> 30:32.748
Sorry about that.

30:32.831 --> 30:36.251
No, don't be sorry.
We used briquettes when I was a kid.

30:37.044 --> 30:39.463
But while getting the used one
out of the heater,

30:39.546 --> 30:44.092
she poked it with red-hot tongs
and ended up with a big burn on her arm.

30:44.885 --> 30:46.887
My goodness.

30:46.970 --> 30:48.180
Oh, dear.

30:50.140 --> 30:53.727
Even now, whenever I see that burn mark,

30:53.810 --> 30:57.105
my heart breaks, you know.

30:59.107 --> 31:03.320
My mother worked so hard to make me,
her son, a mayor.

31:03.987 --> 31:05.322
[sighs]

31:05.405 --> 31:06.740
Her only wish

31:07.866 --> 31:10.911
is to get to live in Beauté Palace
before she passes away.

31:13.163 --> 31:14.372
You know what I mean, right?

31:16.666 --> 31:17.667
Yes, well...

31:18.835 --> 31:20.462
Give me a little time.

31:21.546 --> 31:22.714
I'll see what I can do.

31:23.715 --> 31:25.634
[mayor taps Sungwoo's leg, sighs]

31:25.717 --> 31:28.887
Isn't it a lovely day today?

31:29.888 --> 31:32.057
[♪ tense, dramatic music playing]

32:01.545 --> 32:03.380
Give me a unit at Beauté Palace,

32:03.463 --> 32:06.591
and you won't have to worry
about the permit for the new store.

32:09.010 --> 32:10.595
Life is all about helping each other.

32:11.304 --> 32:13.932
Of course, thank you
for looking out for me.

32:14.599 --> 32:15.642
[chuckles]

32:16.810 --> 32:19.855
The air today is so crisp and fresh.

32:39.291 --> 32:41.209
[sarcastically] What a tearjerker
of a story.

32:41.793 --> 32:42.919
I almost cried.

32:44.296 --> 32:46.464
[in normal tone] Why does he want me
to help out his parents?

32:48.175 --> 32:49.301
Did you look into it?

32:50.260 --> 32:52.512
The company doesn't own
any units right now.

32:52.596 --> 32:54.306
We must wait at least ten months.

32:54.389 --> 32:55.515
What?

32:55.599 --> 32:57.767
You want me to listen to that
for ten more months?

32:59.978 --> 33:01.146
[sighs wearily]

33:02.731 --> 33:03.773
I apologize.

33:03.857 --> 33:06.067
If only we hadn't lost it in the raffle.

33:07.194 --> 33:08.278
Right?

33:09.905 --> 33:11.072
You take care of it.

33:13.283 --> 33:16.328
Hey, do it like you blackmailed
my dad into paying

33:16.411 --> 33:19.497
to send you abroad to study
because you took an exam for me.

33:19.581 --> 33:22.042
Those guts, that desperation.

33:22.125 --> 33:24.836
Where did all that go?
Did you leave them in the US?

33:24.920 --> 33:26.296
You're spoiled now.

33:28.131 --> 33:29.174
Sanghyeon.

33:30.050 --> 33:31.635
What's up with you these days?

33:31.718 --> 33:32.969
[♪ tense, gripping music playing]

33:33.053 --> 33:34.763
You used to be quick on your feet.

33:34.846 --> 33:36.306
Why have you lost your touch?

33:38.391 --> 33:40.477
[sighs] You're getting to me.

33:45.815 --> 33:47.817
MYUNGSOON

33:55.408 --> 33:56.701
[phone vibrates]

33:58.078 --> 33:59.329
[Jingyeong] What are you up to?

34:03.500 --> 34:04.751
[phone vibrating]

34:08.713 --> 34:09.756
[Kim Wooju] Why ask?

34:13.969 --> 34:16.846
[Jingyeong] It's late,
but I wanted to apologize.

34:17.973 --> 34:19.766
I went too far last time.

34:20.558 --> 34:23.436
Sorry for talking to Ms. Yoo
without asking you first.

34:23.520 --> 34:24.646
-[phone vibrates]
-[sighs]

34:26.606 --> 34:28.316
[Kim Wooju] I also lashed out
at you that day.

34:28.400 --> 34:29.693
Sorry.

34:29.776 --> 34:30.986
[phone vibrating]

34:31.069 --> 34:32.445
[♪ soft, gentle music playing]

34:34.572 --> 34:36.283
[Jingyeong] Are you no longer angry, then?

34:38.076 --> 34:41.204
[Kim Wooju] Don't take it to heart.
Just be your usual macho self.

34:42.038 --> 34:43.081
"Macho"?

34:43.873 --> 34:45.792
Wow, really?

34:48.003 --> 34:49.087
[sighs]

34:50.380 --> 34:51.423
Okay.

34:52.007 --> 34:53.883
Let's eat something nice to make up.

34:56.219 --> 34:57.679
[Kim Wooju] I'm not free today.

34:59.222 --> 35:00.348
Is he busy?

35:00.432 --> 35:01.808
[♪ melancholy music playing]

35:03.560 --> 35:05.186
Can I contact Ms. Yoo, then?

35:05.770 --> 35:06.980
I want to apologize to her...

35:10.984 --> 35:12.277
[sighs]

35:18.575 --> 35:19.701
[sighs]

35:20.410 --> 35:23.580
[Kim Wooju] Now is a bad time. Later.

35:35.842 --> 35:37.719
[Sungwoo] Do it like how
you blackmailed my dad into paying

35:37.802 --> 35:40.138
to send you abroad to study
because you took an exam for me.

35:40.221 --> 35:41.264
[♪ tense music playing]

35:41.348 --> 35:44.184
Those guts, that desperation.

35:44.267 --> 35:45.310
Where did all that go?

35:45.393 --> 35:47.687
What's up with you these days?

35:48.563 --> 35:50.357
You used to be quick on your feet.

35:50.440 --> 35:51.900
Why have you lost your touch?

36:05.538 --> 36:06.539
[scanner beeps]

36:06.956 --> 36:09.167
Get one more can.
It's buy one, get one free.

36:10.293 --> 36:13.588
-I see.
-I'll pay for both.

36:13.672 --> 36:14.673
[scanner beeps]

36:16.383 --> 36:17.509
[soda can pops]

36:18.343 --> 36:19.427
[POS beeps]

36:22.931 --> 36:24.224
[sighs contentedly]

36:24.307 --> 36:25.850
[♪ poignant music playing]

36:33.108 --> 36:34.359
[sighs contentedly]

36:36.611 --> 36:38.613
Do you have a lot on your mind today?

36:42.283 --> 36:44.452
You said you jog to clear your head.

36:45.662 --> 36:48.540
I was right behind you.
You didn't know, did you?

36:51.126 --> 36:54.504
I asked so many questions,
and you didn't answer one.

36:57.006 --> 36:58.049
I didn't know.

36:58.508 --> 37:01.052
I felt like running
at full speed today myself.

37:03.179 --> 37:04.431
Was it a bad day?

37:04.973 --> 37:07.517
No, it was the opposite.

37:09.978 --> 37:11.020
It looks like...

37:12.230 --> 37:13.898
they broke up.

37:16.860 --> 37:17.902
Good for you.

37:18.778 --> 37:20.613
That means you have a shot.

37:20.697 --> 37:21.990
Does it?

37:23.992 --> 37:25.994
Then why does it feel so weird?

37:28.621 --> 37:31.249
It must be because I'm seeing him
having a hard time.

37:31.332 --> 37:32.333
What about you?

37:33.918 --> 37:35.003
[inhales deeply]

37:36.963 --> 37:38.131
[sucking teeth]

37:39.090 --> 37:40.091
[knife drawing]

37:41.301 --> 37:43.595
You'll stare a hole through my head.

37:48.099 --> 37:50.018
I was given a tough problem to solve.

37:52.061 --> 37:54.939
I'm looking for a solution,
and it's giving me a headache.

37:55.023 --> 37:57.567
What happens if you can't solve it?
Will you get fired?

37:57.650 --> 37:58.651
[chuckles softly]

37:59.027 --> 38:00.445
Quit before you get fired.

38:00.945 --> 38:03.865
Why worry when you're a competent guy?

38:05.074 --> 38:06.701
There's a reason I can't quit.

38:09.037 --> 38:10.121
[Jingyeong] What's that?

38:10.205 --> 38:13.249
Does your boss have leverage
that he's using to keep you?

38:13.333 --> 38:16.836
You should just take him on, then.

38:16.920 --> 38:18.963
Every company has a few dirty secrets.

38:19.506 --> 38:21.758
Bullying subcontractors,
signing dirty deals,

38:21.841 --> 38:23.134
or stock price manipulation.

38:23.218 --> 38:24.260
There must be something...

38:24.344 --> 38:26.930
I'd be the one to go down
because I did it all.

38:29.182 --> 38:30.308
[chuckles softly]

38:30.391 --> 38:32.018
In your case,

38:32.602 --> 38:34.729
you did as you were told,
it wasn't by choice.

38:38.233 --> 38:39.818
Do you think I was forced into it?

38:40.360 --> 38:41.361
What?

38:44.614 --> 38:46.282
-Well...
-Just kidding.

38:46.950 --> 38:48.117
You're so gullible.

38:49.911 --> 38:51.496
[chuckles] Right?

38:52.622 --> 38:54.707
You almost had me.

38:58.044 --> 38:59.087
[sighs softly]

39:07.679 --> 39:10.974
[Ms. Oh] We have the list of VIPs
to ship the anniversary gifts to.

39:11.057 --> 39:14.519
We need you to engrave the souvenirs
with the right initials,

39:14.602 --> 39:16.354
so double-check once more.

39:16.437 --> 39:17.689
I'll do that.

39:18.523 --> 39:19.566
VIP SOUVENIR PACKAGE

39:24.529 --> 39:25.530
[clears throat]

39:25.613 --> 39:27.490
Shall we end the meeting, then?

39:27.574 --> 39:29.075
-Yes, thank you.
-Thank you.

39:29.158 --> 39:30.201
Great job.

39:30.285 --> 39:31.536
Mr. Kim.

39:31.619 --> 39:35.456
It's Sejung's birthday.
Why don't you join us all for lunch?

39:35.540 --> 39:37.333
-Come with us, Mr. Kim.
-Well...

39:38.293 --> 39:40.503
-[Ms. Oh] What shall we eat?
-[Sejung] How about that place?

39:40.587 --> 39:42.505
-[Ms. Oh] That place?
-[Wonseok] I like that place.

39:42.589 --> 39:43.631
[Sejung] It's my treat.

39:43.715 --> 39:45.216
Shall we go
somewhere else, then?

39:45.300 --> 39:47.427
-[Ms. Oh] No.
-[Wonseok] Let's go to a beef barbecue.

39:47.510 --> 39:50.305
[Songhee] Is the beef barbecue
on you, Ms. Oh?

39:50.388 --> 39:52.140
[Wonseok] Let's go get some beef.

39:52.223 --> 39:53.308
[Ms. Oh] Let's go. It's on me.

39:53.808 --> 39:54.976
Mr. Kim.

39:55.351 --> 39:56.394
Yes.

39:56.811 --> 39:58.146
What about Ms. Yoo?

39:58.229 --> 40:00.189
She has another urgent appointment.

40:00.273 --> 40:02.358
-Out of the blue?
-Yes.

40:02.442 --> 40:05.320
-[Ms. Oh] Is something wrong?
-[Wonseok] I don't know.

40:07.488 --> 40:08.489
Shall we go, Mr. Kim?

40:09.115 --> 40:10.158
Sure.

40:11.576 --> 40:13.494
-[Ms. Oh] Beef.
-[Sejung] I'm excited.

40:13.578 --> 40:14.954
[Ms. Oh] Eat all you want today.

40:15.038 --> 40:16.956
[Sejung] Oh, nice.
Is it your cheat day today?

40:17.540 --> 40:18.791
[Ms. Oh] Yes, eat.

40:19.334 --> 40:20.376
Let's go.

40:29.469 --> 40:32.388
FLOWERS

40:33.139 --> 40:34.140
[chuckles softly]

40:36.976 --> 40:38.436
[♪ wistful pop music playing]

40:42.190 --> 40:43.232
[grunts]

40:50.949 --> 40:52.951
Hey, are you all right?

40:53.034 --> 40:54.619
[sobs, sniffles]

40:59.958 --> 41:01.584
[crying hysterically]

41:21.646 --> 41:23.314
[♪ wistful pop music continues]

41:28.236 --> 41:29.278
[exhales]

41:29.570 --> 41:30.780
[Kim Wooju] Are you all right?

41:34.617 --> 41:35.618
[groans softly]

42:24.333 --> 42:26.502
MYUNGSOON

42:34.343 --> 42:35.553
[line ringing]

42:42.143 --> 42:43.144
[line disconnects]

42:47.857 --> 42:48.900
[sighs softly]

42:48.983 --> 42:50.693
[♪ gentle, poignant music playing]

44:06.936 --> 44:07.979
Hello.

44:08.437 --> 44:10.523
-Mr. Kim.
-Yes?

44:12.024 --> 44:13.860
There's something you should see.

44:14.485 --> 44:15.570
[inhales deeply]

44:19.907 --> 44:24.996
He brought a letter
and insisted on seeing the chairwoman.

44:26.205 --> 44:28.583
I swore the employees to secrecy.

44:30.418 --> 44:32.086
[♪ tense, gripping music playing]

44:34.797 --> 44:36.382
[guard] Before he left,

44:36.465 --> 44:39.260
he asked about your relationship
with the chairwoman.

44:42.430 --> 44:44.891
Did he figure something out?

44:48.686 --> 44:50.313
MYUNGSOON

44:50.396 --> 44:51.522
[line ringing]

44:51.606 --> 44:54.442
[automated voice] The call cannot
be connected. Transferring to voicemail.

44:54.525 --> 44:56.068
Oh, come on.

44:59.906 --> 45:00.948
[tires screeching]

45:11.375 --> 45:12.877
I did as you asked.

45:13.294 --> 45:14.337
Are you sure?

45:14.420 --> 45:15.838
See for yourself if you don't believe me.

45:17.715 --> 45:18.716
[sighs softly]

45:21.135 --> 45:22.595
So, don't do anything to him.

45:22.678 --> 45:24.263
He's got nothing to do with me now.

45:26.849 --> 45:29.644
I have no reason to
if he has nothing to do with you.

45:32.271 --> 45:33.314
Now...

45:37.693 --> 45:38.736
Let's talk about us.

45:41.739 --> 45:43.741
With him gone, we can start over.

45:43.824 --> 45:45.493
What are you talking about?

45:46.619 --> 45:49.247
Why would I get back with you
because I broke up with him?

46:00.174 --> 46:01.259
What are you doing?

46:01.759 --> 46:02.802
Meri.

46:03.302 --> 46:05.179
I regret everything I did.

46:05.263 --> 46:08.224
I was a real fool and a jerk.

46:09.517 --> 46:10.559
I was a jerk! [slaps self]

46:11.477 --> 46:13.271
I shouldn't have done that to you!

46:13.729 --> 46:15.231
I repaid your love with betrayal.

46:16.190 --> 46:19.110
My point is, I want another chance.

46:19.193 --> 46:20.861
This isn't our deal.

46:21.654 --> 46:23.948
You said you wouldn't report or bother me
if I broke up with him.

46:24.031 --> 46:26.784
How am I bothering you?
I just want you back.

46:28.119 --> 46:29.287
Forget all about him

46:29.954 --> 46:33.249
and live happily in this house with me.

46:34.333 --> 46:36.085
There's a famous French proverb.

46:36.544 --> 46:38.421
[in French] Après la pluie, le beau temps.

46:38.504 --> 46:40.798
[in Korean] It basically means
sunshine comes after rain.

46:41.340 --> 46:43.801
What happened
will make our relationship stronger.

46:44.593 --> 46:47.471
-I'll make it up to you.
-Will you stop it?

46:47.555 --> 46:48.889
We can't keep the house.

46:50.516 --> 46:51.559
Why not?

46:53.394 --> 46:54.395
[chuckles]

46:54.478 --> 46:57.231
I won't report you.
The department store won't know.

46:57.315 --> 46:59.817
-You can keep the house.
-Even if you don't report me,

47:00.735 --> 47:01.944
I'll report myself.

47:02.903 --> 47:05.489
-What?
-I'll tell the director right now.

47:05.573 --> 47:07.158
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

47:08.451 --> 47:09.493
You can't.

47:10.077 --> 47:11.120
Let go.

47:16.250 --> 47:17.376
Have you lost your mind?

47:17.460 --> 47:18.836
You want to give up a fortune?

47:18.919 --> 47:20.504
It's mine. I can do what I want.

47:22.131 --> 47:25.426
Hey, how is it yours? Half of it is mine.

47:25.509 --> 47:26.886
Who says you can give it up?

47:26.969 --> 47:29.055
You abuse me to the very end.

47:29.972 --> 47:31.849
You want me back for the house, don't you?

47:31.932 --> 47:33.851
[scoffs] That's not the issue.

47:34.435 --> 47:36.520
I'll have you and this house.

47:36.604 --> 47:38.522
Don't you even dream of coming clean.

47:38.606 --> 47:41.192
I'll make you pay if you call the police.
I'll make Kim Wooju pay, too.

47:41.275 --> 47:42.401
[angrily] Leave him alone!

47:42.485 --> 47:44.987
That was when you were eligible
to keep this house!

47:46.238 --> 47:47.281
Hey.

47:48.115 --> 47:49.700
You're off to see him, aren't you?

47:50.493 --> 47:51.660
Was all that a show?

47:52.161 --> 47:53.662
Did you pretend to dump him to silence me?

47:55.039 --> 47:56.082
You're insane.

47:57.333 --> 47:58.334
Why, you...

48:04.423 --> 48:07.176
If you want to threaten someone,
do that to me.

48:08.094 --> 48:09.136
You should be ashamed.

48:09.720 --> 48:10.846
-[bone cracking]
-[exclaims]

48:12.973 --> 48:14.016
Mr. Kim.

48:15.601 --> 48:16.644
[Kim Wooju] Ms. Yoo.

48:16.727 --> 48:18.604
Hand in the divorce decree tomorrow.

48:19.647 --> 48:21.357
So he can't interfere anymore.

48:22.650 --> 48:24.902
If you want to report us, go ahead.

48:25.569 --> 48:26.737
I'll pay for what I did.

48:27.238 --> 48:28.280
[Wooju] What?

48:29.115 --> 48:30.116
You'll pay?

48:34.578 --> 48:35.579
[grunts]

48:39.750 --> 48:42.086
You can do whatever you want.

48:42.878 --> 48:45.339
But stay away from Ms. Yoo.

48:51.011 --> 48:53.556
How dare a fraud show up and lecture me?

48:54.223 --> 48:57.518
You're accomplices in this!

48:59.728 --> 49:00.813
What about you, then?

49:01.230 --> 49:02.731
What about me?

49:05.317 --> 49:06.444
[Wooju] That's not the issue.

49:06.527 --> 49:08.654
I'll have you and this house.

49:08.737 --> 49:11.031
Don't you even dream of coming clean.

49:11.115 --> 49:13.284
I'll make you pay if you call the police.
I'll make Kim Wooju pay, too

49:13.367 --> 49:14.577
[Meri angrily] Leave him alone!

49:14.660 --> 49:15.703
What do you say?

49:16.537 --> 49:17.746
You're not involved now?

49:20.040 --> 49:21.375
[♪ music increases in tempo, fades]

49:23.502 --> 49:24.587
[exclaims in frustration]

49:40.436 --> 49:42.104
[♪ tense music playing]

49:50.070 --> 49:51.155
[gate clatters]

49:57.870 --> 49:58.913
Wait and see.

50:00.206 --> 50:01.790
I'll make you both pay.

50:14.678 --> 50:17.932
[sighs softly] You should've told me
if that had happened.

50:18.015 --> 50:19.433
What were you going to do on your own?

50:20.059 --> 50:21.310
It's all my fault.

50:23.479 --> 50:25.981
I didn't want to bother you again.

50:27.483 --> 50:30.986
Please... please
don't say stuff like that.

50:31.654 --> 50:33.197
[♪ gentle, dreamy music playing]

50:33.280 --> 50:36.367
Do you know how rough it was for me
after you walked off?

50:37.952 --> 50:39.828
Not being with you is the worst.

50:45.334 --> 50:46.752
Also...

50:47.628 --> 50:50.839
Stop saying you want
to break up for my sake.

50:52.925 --> 50:54.593
If you really care about me,

50:55.511 --> 50:57.137
stay right next to me.

51:00.599 --> 51:02.434
Even if it's just for a day,

51:03.269 --> 51:05.145
I want to be with you.

51:07.314 --> 51:08.357
So...

51:10.025 --> 51:12.027
stay by my side.

51:13.487 --> 51:14.530
That day...

51:17.950 --> 51:20.369
[sniffles] I'm sorry I was so harsh.

51:52.693 --> 51:54.862
-Mr. Kim.
-Yes?

51:56.530 --> 51:58.490
It's the VIP guest list

51:58.574 --> 52:00.784
-for the 80th anniversary event.
-I see.

52:02.328 --> 52:03.537
[hums thoughtfully]

52:04.288 --> 52:06.040
BEAUTÉ DEPARTMENT STORE

52:06.373 --> 52:07.583
[♪ dramatic sting]

52:10.044 --> 52:11.754
Beauté Department Store?

52:11.837 --> 52:14.548
You invited people from Beauté?
They weren't on the initial list.

52:14.632 --> 52:17.718
Oh, Director Jang contacted them himself.

52:17.801 --> 52:20.804
The secretary's office called,
so we updated the guest list.

52:21.722 --> 52:23.557
[acknowledges, chuckles nervously]

52:24.933 --> 52:26.977
Okay, then. Thanks.

52:27.061 --> 52:28.228
Sure.

52:30.439 --> 52:31.482
[sighs]

52:32.066 --> 52:33.442
Will they come?

52:33.525 --> 52:34.568
Sorry.

52:35.194 --> 52:37.905
Mr. Lee and I are going
to Japan on business.

52:37.988 --> 52:39.990
We won't be able to attend.

52:40.908 --> 52:41.950
Bye.

52:43.035 --> 52:44.036
[line disconnects]

52:44.161 --> 52:45.329
Was that Myungsoondang?

52:45.704 --> 52:46.747
Yes.

52:49.541 --> 52:50.751
Send a flower arrangement.

52:51.585 --> 52:52.628
Yes, sir.

53:02.513 --> 53:03.555
[David] Director Baek?

53:05.224 --> 53:07.184
Oh, Kaltz Hotel...

53:07.267 --> 53:09.103
[in English] It's really you.

53:09.812 --> 53:10.896
[in Korean] It's been a while.

53:10.979 --> 53:13.065
-Are you headed to Japan?
-[Sanghyeon] Yes, on business.

53:13.732 --> 53:14.775
What about you?

53:14.858 --> 53:16.568
I quit the hotel business.

53:16.652 --> 53:19.530
I'm based in Tokyo now,
where I'm planning a new enterprise.

53:19.613 --> 53:21.198
I visited Korea briefly.

53:21.281 --> 53:22.616
Oh, I see.

53:22.700 --> 53:24.576
-[passenger] Excuse me.
-[in English] Oh, sorry.

53:24.660 --> 53:27.079
-Then, good luck to your business.
-Thanks.

53:32.418 --> 53:34.628
-Who was that?
-Oh, him?

53:35.212 --> 53:37.631
When I was based in the US five years ago,

53:37.715 --> 53:40.050
we met once or twice
at a Korean get-together.

53:40.134 --> 53:42.136
It's David Lee
who worked at the Kaltz Hotel.

53:42.219 --> 53:44.012
It looks like he quit.

53:55.816 --> 53:57.317
CEO
KO PHILNYUN

53:57.401 --> 53:59.820
Be sure to send a gift

53:59.903 --> 54:02.072
and call those who can't attend.

54:03.115 --> 54:04.783
Yes, I'll do that.

54:07.202 --> 54:09.121
Also, bring the person you want to invite.

54:10.164 --> 54:12.708
-Sorry?
-You chose her over Jingyeong.

54:13.125 --> 54:14.835
I wonder what family she's from.

54:15.294 --> 54:16.628
Is it a family I know?

54:16.712 --> 54:18.422
Gosh, no.

54:20.632 --> 54:22.509
You'll love her when you see her.

54:23.135 --> 54:24.470
She's really pretty.

54:25.387 --> 54:26.430
Oh, but...

54:27.514 --> 54:30.476
Word got out that you're really picky.

54:30.559 --> 54:32.478
[loudly] That's not true at all!

54:34.396 --> 54:37.024
[in neutral tone] So what?
She doesn't like us?

54:37.107 --> 54:39.693
No, it's not like that at all.

54:39.777 --> 54:43.113
Tell the young lady
you have no mother to bully her

54:43.197 --> 54:45.199
and that your grandma is old and frail.

54:45.699 --> 54:48.494
She can eat all the pastries she wants
if she marries you.

54:48.577 --> 54:49.995
Wait, what?

54:50.078 --> 54:52.331
You make me pay for everything I eat.

54:52.414 --> 54:53.457
Well, you...

54:53.540 --> 54:55.125
[♪ feel-good music playing]

54:55.209 --> 54:57.586
I'll think about it
if you give me a grandchild.

54:57.669 --> 54:58.837
What?

54:58.921 --> 55:00.464
[softly] Oh, goodness...

55:01.048 --> 55:02.508
-Madam Scrooge.
-How dare you?

55:03.383 --> 55:04.468
[in neutral tone] Fine.

55:04.551 --> 55:07.721
If that's what you want, I'll ask her.

55:13.143 --> 55:14.853
The chairwoman asked?

55:14.937 --> 55:16.021
Yes.

55:16.104 --> 55:17.648
Grandma's been really curious about you.

55:19.733 --> 55:22.569
What if we meet
the people from Beauté there?

55:22.653 --> 55:24.821
Do you think
I didn't check that beforehand?

55:25.280 --> 55:26.532
Don't worry.

55:26.615 --> 55:29.076
I asked, and they said they couldn't come.

55:29.159 --> 55:31.119
Oh, did they?

55:31.203 --> 55:32.579
Yes.

55:32.663 --> 55:33.914
So, dress up nicely.

55:34.540 --> 55:36.750
-Not that you need to try to look pretty.
-[chuckles]

55:36.833 --> 55:38.043
[♪ whimsical music playing]

55:38.126 --> 55:39.378
I'll try.

55:40.420 --> 55:41.588
Sleep well.

55:41.672 --> 55:42.714
Okay.

55:44.424 --> 55:45.425
[line disconnects]

56:01.775 --> 56:02.776
[Miyeon] Thank you.

56:03.443 --> 56:05.529
-[guest 1] Congratulations.
-[Philnyun] Yes, thank you.

56:06.113 --> 56:08.115
-[Hangu] Hello.
-Oh, you made it.

56:08.198 --> 56:09.783
-Thank you.
-[guest 2] Congratulations.

56:09.866 --> 56:11.910
[♪ soft classic music
playing in background]

56:12.244 --> 56:13.704
Oh, thank you for coming.

56:35.934 --> 56:36.977
Ms. Yoo.

56:39.646 --> 56:40.856
Why are you out here?

56:40.939 --> 56:43.400
I was a bit nervous.

56:43.483 --> 56:44.693
Why would you be?

56:45.193 --> 56:47.863
The others should be nervous
to be around your beauty.

56:47.946 --> 56:49.281
[both chuckle]

56:49.364 --> 56:50.574
Come on inside.

56:54.995 --> 56:57.205
-[guest 3] Congratulations.
-Thank you.

56:57.289 --> 56:58.290
[chuckles]

57:02.085 --> 57:03.295
Chairwoman.

57:03.378 --> 57:05.297
-[Philnyun] Oh, hi.
-Hello.

57:05.380 --> 57:06.506
Hello, Ms. Yoo.

57:06.590 --> 57:08.383
Congratulations on the anniversary.

57:08.467 --> 57:09.509
Thank you.

57:09.968 --> 57:11.345
Take her to her seat, Mr. Kim.

57:11.428 --> 57:12.596
Yes, of course.

57:13.055 --> 57:14.139
But...

57:15.932 --> 57:17.851
-About what I said before--
-[Juhee] Chairwoman.

57:17.934 --> 57:19.436
The undersecretary is here.

57:19.519 --> 57:20.562
[Philnyun] Okay.

57:29.237 --> 57:31.281
[chuckles softly] Shall we talk later?

57:32.282 --> 57:33.283
Yes.

57:37.287 --> 57:38.580
[Philnyun] Thanks for coming.

57:39.164 --> 57:40.582
-Thank you.
-Let's go inside.

57:42.751 --> 57:45.212
[Sejung] Park Jaegwan,
Quality Management Team.

57:45.295 --> 57:46.546
[♪ upbeat, whimsical music playing]

57:46.630 --> 57:48.632
Gang Giseong, Design Team.

57:49.216 --> 57:51.635
Han Wonseok, Marketing Team.

57:53.261 --> 57:54.513
Thank you!

57:54.596 --> 57:57.557
[Sejung] Kim Jingyu,
Research and Development Team.

57:57.641 --> 58:01.853
Nine people were awarded the long-term
service award for their ten-year tenure.

58:01.937 --> 58:04.064
Please give them some warm applause.

58:09.152 --> 58:10.153
EXECUTIVES

58:19.454 --> 58:23.375
Now, Chairwoman Ko Philnyun
will give a speech.

58:24.459 --> 58:26.712
Please give her a warm welcome.

58:26.795 --> 58:28.171
[all applauding, cheering]

58:43.061 --> 58:44.229
[grunts]

58:51.027 --> 58:52.529
Eighty years...

58:54.030 --> 58:56.867
is long enough for our surroundings
to change many times.

58:56.950 --> 58:58.994
Over that long time,

58:59.077 --> 59:04.040
our Myungsoondang has been through
many changes and ups and downs.

59:05.500 --> 59:06.501
LEE SUNGWOO

59:06.585 --> 59:08.712
If there's one thing that doesn't change,

59:09.546 --> 59:10.589
that would be...

59:11.089 --> 59:13.884
-Hello?
-...the spirit of care and sharing.

59:13.967 --> 59:15.051
That's great to hear.

59:15.135 --> 59:19.306
-I hope to see you soon. Bye.
-I learned from my late mother-in-law

59:19.389 --> 59:22.225
-the spirit of care and sharing.
-[line ringing]

59:22.309 --> 59:25.228
-Set up two more seats at the VIP table...
-My mother-in-law

59:25.312 --> 59:27.898
-[Hangu] ...for Beauté's people.
-[Philnyun] left me a great legacy.

59:27.981 --> 59:32.444
I clung to that spirit,
and it brought us this far.

59:33.069 --> 59:36.448
I believe that's why
you shower us with your love.

59:36.782 --> 59:37.783
[phone vibrates]

59:37.866 --> 59:40.410
In the future, we must take this spirit...

59:40.494 --> 59:43.330
[Kim Wooju] Ms. Yoo,
Mr. Baek is on his way here.

59:43.413 --> 59:44.998
[Philnyun] Not forgetting that

59:45.081 --> 59:48.210
is the way to repay you
for your appreciation.

59:49.336 --> 59:53.507
I thank you again for sparing
your precious time to join us.

59:53.590 --> 59:55.091
[guests cheering, applauding]

59:57.010 --> 59:59.304
What happened?
You said they couldn't come.

59:59.387 --> 01:00:01.556
Their business trip got cut short.

01:00:02.182 --> 01:00:03.225
What should we do?

01:00:03.308 --> 01:00:07.062
Well, we decided to come clean.
Why don't we just do that today?

01:00:07.687 --> 01:00:10.565
We should tell the chairwoman first.

01:00:10.649 --> 01:00:12.901
It's not right
to let her hear it from Mr. Baek.

01:00:13.443 --> 01:00:14.778
What do we do, then?

01:00:15.320 --> 01:00:18.615
I think we should avoid
crossing paths with Mr. Baek.

01:00:18.698 --> 01:00:20.367
Only until we tell the chairwoman.

01:00:20.992 --> 01:00:22.077
Let's do that.

01:00:22.160 --> 01:00:23.662
Go ahead. I'll say goodbye first.

01:00:24.830 --> 01:00:26.623
[♪ gripping, whimsical music playing]

01:01:03.910 --> 01:01:06.454
-[guest] You look amazing.
-[Philnyun chuckles] Thank you.

01:01:12.210 --> 01:01:14.838
-Hello.
-Are you going somewhere?

01:01:15.922 --> 01:01:20.176
I need to be somewhere. I'm so sorry.

01:01:20.260 --> 01:01:21.553
Okay.

01:01:22.304 --> 01:01:24.389
I was hoping to speak with you.

01:01:25.849 --> 01:01:28.935
Are you personally close to my Wooju?

01:01:30.896 --> 01:01:31.938
[hesitating]

01:01:32.898 --> 01:01:34.024
Yes.

01:01:34.774 --> 01:01:38.069
Team Manager Kim Wooju is my grandson.
You know that, right?

01:01:38.653 --> 01:01:40.030
[Meri] Yes, I know.

01:01:40.113 --> 01:01:43.408
[Philnyun] If you're busy today,
you should visit me at home one day.

01:01:46.620 --> 01:01:47.704
[chuckles softly]

01:01:53.877 --> 01:01:54.920
[chuckles softly]

01:02:12.687 --> 01:02:14.439
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

01:02:28.495 --> 01:02:29.871
[line ringing]

01:02:30.330 --> 01:02:31.414
Yes, sir.

01:02:31.998 --> 01:02:35.043
I think I can secure a unit
for the mayor of Yongdu soon.

01:02:35.543 --> 01:02:38.755
I may be able to retrieve the house
that was lost through the raffle.

01:02:43.593 --> 01:02:44.970
[♪ music crescendos, fades]

01:02:52.102 --> 01:02:53.228
Mr. Baek.

01:02:57.148 --> 01:02:59.693
Thank you so much for coming.

01:03:00.110 --> 01:03:01.736
Come on in.

01:03:01.820 --> 01:03:02.821
Mr. Kim.

01:03:03.363 --> 01:03:05.115
What's your relationship with Ms. Yoo?

01:03:06.866 --> 01:03:09.411
Are you two really married?

01:03:09.494 --> 01:03:11.079
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

01:03:11.162 --> 01:03:12.247
[hesitates]

01:03:23.299 --> 01:03:24.300
[hesitates]

01:03:34.978 --> 01:03:36.563
[♪ gentle pop music playing]

01:03:44.029 --> 01:03:46.656
THANKS TO KIM YOUNGJAE
FOR THE SPECIAL APPEARANCE

01:04:01.796 --> 01:04:04.799
WOULD YOU MARRY ME?

01:04:04.883 --> 01:04:07.218
[Sanghyeon] If not married,
the prize will be revoked.

01:04:07.302 --> 01:04:09.095
[Jingyeong] I'm left with no choice, then.

01:04:09.179 --> 01:04:10.472
I have no choice but to reveal.

01:04:10.555 --> 01:04:14.017
[Meri] If someone gives you a hard time,
I won't stand for it.

01:04:14.100 --> 01:04:15.894
[Juhee] The chairwoman
probably didn't know

01:04:16.186 --> 01:04:18.438
that the contract with the Kaltz was fake.

01:04:18.521 --> 01:04:20.732
[Meri] This person...
She said her name was Jessica.

01:04:20.815 --> 01:04:22.567
[Eungsoo] Grandma woke up?

01:04:22.650 --> 01:04:24.069
[Kim Wooju] It's all over now.

01:04:24.861 --> 01:04:26.905
Grandma, I'm afraid.

01:04:27.530 --> 01:04:29.199
I'm afraid that you were right.

01:04:29.908 --> 01:04:30.909
Was it you, Uncle?

01:04:30.992 --> 01:04:32.077
[exclaims in frustration]

01:04:33.119 --> 01:04:34.496
[Kim Wooju] Was it you?

01:04:37.290 --> 01:04:39.292
Translated by Jennifer Jean Lim
